>> title: Ful Medames, Instant Pot
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: fava beans, egyptian, breakfast, cumin, vegan, instant pot, pressure cooker, no soak
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot ful medames, pressure cooker ful, no soak fava beans, foul medames, ful mudammas, fool medames, fava beans, Egyptian breakfast beans
>> servings: 4
>> dish: ful-medames
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: pita-bread, labneh, kabis
>> time: 1 hr 35 min
>> step.1: dry beans straight in, no soak — pressure cook 45 min
>> step.2: natural release 20 min
>> step.3: crush about half against the pot
>> step.4: dress with lemon, oil and cumin
>> step.5: build the top, finish at the table

Put @dried fava beans{1 1/2%cups}(300 g; small brown ful, dry — not soaked, not the big pale broad bean) into the #Instant Pot{} with @water{5%cups}(1.2 L), @bay leaf{1} and @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, lock the lid and ~pressure cook{45%min} at high pressure. This is the whole reason to own the pot: the plain version wants the beans in water the night before, and this one starts when you are hungry. Forty-five minutes is for the small brown bean with its skin on, which is a tougher bean than the peeled broad bean sold for salads — that one is done in half the time and is the wrong bean anyway.

Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops on its own. Never vent a pot of beans: the pressure drops faster than the liquid inside the beans can, and they burst their skins on the way out. The beans should flatten under a spoon with no resistance at all. If they do not, lock the lid and give them another ten minutes — undercooked beans do not come right later.

Crush about half of @&(~1)cooked beans{} against the side of the inner pot with a spoon and leave the rest whole, ladling off most of the water first and stirring a little back in. Half crushed and half whole is the texture; a full mash is hummus and a pan of loose beans is soup.

Dress @&(~1)crushed beans{} with @lemon juice{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @extra-virgin olive oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed to a paste), @ground cumin{2%tsp} and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}, stirring hard so it goes glossy. All of it goes in now, after the pressure and not before — salt and lemon in with dry beans slow them down and you will be back to guessing at the time.

Turn @&(~1)dressed ful{} into a shallow bowl and build @ripe tomato{1}(diced), @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped), @red onion{1/4}(diced fine) and @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) over the top, with @lemon{1}(in wedges) and more cumin alongside. It arrives undressed on purpose and every table finishes it differently — that is the meal, not a serving suggestion.
